{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the parameter prior sampling statements so that each parameter is sampled before it is used by another prior or by the likelihood. This is a mechanical same-density change because the model log density is a sum of the same built-in distribution terms. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;      // Number of observations
  vector[N] y;         // Observations
  real<lower=0> sigma; // Measurement variability

  // Number of individual contexts
  int<lower=0> K;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> obs_to_context;

  // Factor information
  int<lower=0> N_factor_levels;
  array[K] int<lower=1, upper=N_factor_levels> context_to_level;
}

parameters {
  // Centered hierarchical models for the conditional heterogeneity within each level
  vector[K] context_theta;                       // Centered individual parameters
  vector<lower=0>[N_factor_levels] residual_tau; // Population scales within each level

  // Centered hierarchical model for the marginal level heterogeneity
  vector[N_factor_levels] factor_theta; // Centered individual parameters
  real factor_mu;                       // Population location
  real<lower=0> factor_tau;             // Population scale
}

model {
  factor_mu ~ normal(0, 5);
  factor_tau ~ normal(0, 3);
  factor_theta ~ normal(factor_mu, factor_tau);

  residual_tau ~ normal(0, 3);
  context_theta ~ normal(factor_theta[context_to_level],
                         residual_tau[context_to_level]);

  y ~ normal(context_theta[obs_to_context], sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":2,"N":4,"N_factor_levels":4,"context_to_level":[1,4],"obs_to_context":[2,1,2,1],"sigma":0.859119403020085,"y":[3.0,4.0,4.0,4.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
